<title>UK: HORSE RACING-JULY CUP RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-JULY CUP RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>NEWMARKET, England 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the July</p>
<p>Cup, a group one race for three-year-olds and upwards run over</p>
<p>six furlongs (1.2 kms) on Thursday:</p>
<p>1. Compton Place 50-1 (ridden by Seb Sanders)</p>
<p>2. Royal Applause 11-10 favourite (Michael Hills)</p>
<p>3. Indian Rocket 9-1 (Richard Hills)</p>
<p>9 ran</p>
<p>Distances: One length, three lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by the Duke of Devonshire and trained by James</p>
<p>Toller in England.</p>
<p>Value to winner: 92,270 pounds ($155,000)</p>
</text>
